nvolving plant cells at low pH.\nL202: ### Application\nL203:   * Evaluation of buffers toxicity in plant cells: Homopiperazine-1,4-bis(2-ethanesulfonic acid) was evaluated for its suitability as a buffer in tobacco cell studies at low pH, highlighting its low toxicity and effectiveness in maintaining stable pH environments crucial for plant cell biology experiments (【16†Borgo, 2017†doi.org】).\nL204:   * Proteomic analysis under stress conditions: This buffer was used in maintaining pH during the proteomic analysis of radicles from seeds treated with aluminum, showcasing its utility in complex biological assays and environmental stress studies (【17†Okekeogbu et al., 2014†doi.org】).\nL205: * * *\nL206: \nL207: * * *\nL208: ## Safety Information\nL209: \nL210: ### Pictograms\nL211: \nL212: 【18†GHS05,GHS07】\nL213: \nL214: ### Signal Word\nL215: \nL216: Danger\nL217: \nL218: ### Hazard Codes\nL219: \nL220: 【19†H312,H314】\nL221: \nL222: ### Precautionary Statements\nL223: \nL224: 【20†P260 - P280 - P303 + P361 + P353 - P304 + P340 + P310 - P305 + P351 + P338 - P362 + P364】\nL225: \nL226: ### Hazard Classifications\nL227: \nL228: Acute Tox. 4 Dermal - Skin Corr. 1B\nL229: \nL230: ### Storage Class\nL231: \nL232: 8A - Combustible corrosive hazardous materials\nL233: \nL234: ### WGK\nL235: \nL236: WGK 3\nL237: \nL238: ### Flash Point (°F)\nL239: \nL240: Not applicable\nL241: \nL242: ### Flash Point (°C)\nL243: \nL244: Not applicable\nL245: ### PPE (personal protective equipment)\nL246: \nL247: Eyeshields, Faceshields, Gloves, type P3 (EN 143) respirator cartridges\nL248: \nL249: * * *\nL250: \nL251: ## Documentation\nL252: \nL253: [Button: Certificate of Analysis][Button: Certificate of Origin]\nL254: \nL255: * * *\nL256: \nL257: Choose from one of the most recent versions:\nL258: \nL259: ### Certificates of Analysis (COA)\nL260: \nL261: Lot/Batch Number\nL262: \nL263: It looks like we've run into a problem, but you can still download Certificates of Analysis from our 【21†Do